    "review_depth": "Official parent and exact CPU variation cards, repository migration notice, Hoplite README and pinned model configuration reviewed. The full arXiv HTML for Burns et al. (2025), sections 1â€“6 and its methods/results, was also reviewed. No weights, code, or evaluation datasets were acquired or run.",
    "finding": "Perch v2 provides acoustic embeddings for downstream classifiers. The official CPU version 1 card declares Apache-2.0 and says its weights match the GPU perch_v2 version 2. Pinned Hoplite configuration uses five-second, mono 32 kHz windows and a 1,536-dimensional embedding. Burns et al. (2025) report strong few-shot linear-probe classification across marine datasets using Perch 2.0 embeddings; this supports transferable acoustic features for bounded classification tasks.",
    "limitations": "The transfer paper evaluates species/ecotype or broad sound classes, not call meaning or communication. Its few-shot method randomly selects recording-level examples and does not establish site-, deployment-, session- or individual-held-out generalization. The paper says these tasks were among Perch 2.0's development validation sources, while separately describing DCLDE as unseen; exact model-selection overlap needs clarification before treating scores as a blind independent test. It reports around a dozen cetacean training recordings, mostly above-water phone audio, not hydrophone recordings. The card names Xeno-Canto, iNaturalist, Animal Sound Archive and FSD50k as training sources, but item-level training-data and license provenance, target-data overlap and scientific fit remain unverified. No bundle checksum, runtime, accuracy or mobile performance was verified.",
    "seo_description": "Perch 2.0 embeddings transfer to whale sound classification; this is evidence about acoustic categories, not meaning. Model and dataset rights remain separate.",
    "lesson": "A broad pretrained bioacoustic model can be a starting feature extractor; it does not supply a grounded animal-language system. Compare it with simple baselines on a narrow, rights-cleared task with group-aware evaluation.",
    "next_review": "Before selecting this baseline, verify the exact package integrity and applicable download terms, inspect preprocessing and model-selection overlap, then measure a CPU inference path on synthetic or rights-cleared audio. Keep behavior/context benchmark admission gated on independently reviewed labels and leakage-safe splits.",
